{
  "id": "PPA-05",
  "title": "Reactive Oxygen Species (ROS) & Redox Homeostasis",
  "subtitle": "Superoxide generation, dismutation, the Foyer-Halliwell-Asada cycle, catalases, and thioredoxin relays",
  "caption": "Spatial and biochemical architecture of plant reactive oxygen species (ROS) metabolism. Covers apoplastic oxidative bursts catalyzed by respiratory burst oxidase homologs (RBOHD/F), superoxide dismutation by compartment-specific SOD isoforms (Cu/Zn-SOD, Fe-SOD, Mn-SOD), peroxide detoxification via the ascorbate-glutathione cycle (APX, MDHAR, DHAR, GR) and peroxisomal catalases, and downstream thioredoxin/glutaredoxin redox switches.",
